<div id="2026-09-12-inventory-count-sheet" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-12 — Physical Inventory Count (stock-take) sheet at /Inventory/count</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> New physical count sheet. Filters by SiteName + inventory category; per-item columns show System Qty (g), a Found Qty input + unit select (g/kg/each, with 1 each = 1000 g = 1 kg), computed grams, difference, and note. Save draft (persisted) and Submit (applies) actions. Submit merges duplicate location rows by summing, sets quantity_on_hand to the entered grams, and logs a physical_count transaction for the delta. Built to clean up the early double-location filament rows and give an accurate starting stock across sites/categories.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> User needed a filterable physical count form (tablet-friendly, save-and-resume) to correct stock of record after duplicate-location pollution, before trusting low-stock numbers. Stock is stored canonically in grams; the unit select keeps PO/order vs system units explicit.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Controller/Inventory.pm</code> (inventory_count GET, count_save POST draft, count_submit POST apply, _count_persist helper), <code>Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Accounting/InventoryCountSession.pm</code> (new), <code>Model/Schema/Ency.pm</code> (register), <code>root/Inventory/count.tt</code> (new), <code>root/Inventory/index.tt</code> (📋 Physical Count nav link).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Pending.</strong> The <code>inventory_count_sessions</code> DB table is NOT yet created (needs schema-compare / DDL on the live ency DB). The page renders and filters, but Save/Submit 500 until the table exists. Tablet time-logging of count duration is in the plan but not yet wired.</p>
</div>
